    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0267" n="95" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg95"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/4455</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-27T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 27, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3834. Your 4925. Hale’s statement without any foundation. Your reference to
                    memorandum not clear but no memorandum has been presented and no change of
                    policy is contemplated in regard to armed merchantmen.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
